    {
      "id": "b8786f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Students must earn a \"C-\" grade or higher in all courses required in the major. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Child and Adolescent Development, the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Psychology, and the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Sociology are compatible with the B.S. in Family Studies and Human Development at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. For additional information, please visit: Department of Family and Consumer Sciences .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">Students must earn a \"C-\" grade or higher in all courses required in the major. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Child and Adolescent Development, the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Psychology, and the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Sociology are compatible with the B.S. in Family Studies and Human Development at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/social-sciences-interdisciplinary-studies/family-consumer-sciences/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of Family and Consumer Sciences</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">.</span></li></ol>"
